  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Solve the following by rewriting as $ax^2+bx+c=0$ then using the quadratic formula.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$3x^2=1+6x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{3\\pm2\\sqrt3}{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x^2-6x-1&=0\\\\a&=3,\\quad b=-6,\\quad c=-1\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-6)\\pm\\sqrt{(-6)^2-4(3)(-1)}}{2(3)}\\\\x&=\\frac{6\\pm\\sqrt{48}}6\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pm2\\sqrt3}3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2x^2=3-4x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{10}}2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+4x-3&=0\\\\a&=2,\\quad b=4,\\quad c=-3\\\\x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{4^2-4(2)(-3)}}{2(2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{40}}4\\\\x&=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{10}}2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$5x=2-4x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{57}}8$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4x^2+5x-2&=0\\\\a&=4,\\quad b=5,\\quad c=-2\\\\x&=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{5^2-4(4)(-2)}}{2(4)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{57}}8\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$2x-5=-\\dfrac1x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}4$. Multiply by $x$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2-5x&=-1\\\\2x^2-5x+1&=0\\\\a&=2,\\quad b=-5,\\quad c=1\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-5)\\pm\\sqrt{(-5)^2-4(2)(1)}}{2(2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}4\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac3x=3x+4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{13}}3$. Multiply by $x$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3&=3x^2+4x\\\\3x^2+4x-3&=0\\\\a&=3,\\quad b=4,\\quad c=-3\\\\x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{4^2-4(3)(-3)}}{2(3)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{52}}6\\\\x&=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{13}}3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$-\\dfrac5x=2-x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1\\pm\\sqrt6$. Multiply by $x$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}-5&=2x-x^2\\\\x^2-2x-5&=0\\\\a&=1,\\quad b=-2,\\quad c=-5\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-2)\\pm\\sqrt{(-2)^2-4(1)(-5)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{24}}2\\\\x&=1\\pm\\sqrt6\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$5x=\\dfrac{2x+2}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{1\\pm\\sqrt{11}}5$. Multiply by $x$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}5x^2&=2x+2\\\\5x^2-2x-2&=0\\\\a&=5,\\quad b=-2,\\quad c=-2\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-2)\\pm\\sqrt{(-2)^2-4(5)(-2)}}{2(5)}\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{44}}{10}\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{11}}5\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$x=\\dfrac{3x+4}{2x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{3\\pm\\sqrt{41}}4$. Multiply by $2x$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2&=3x+4\\\\2x^2-3x-4&=0\\\\a&=2,\\quad b=-3,\\quad c=-4\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-3)\\pm\\sqrt{(-3)^2-4(2)(-4)}}{2(2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{41}}4\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$3x=\\dfrac{10x-1}{2x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{5\\pm\\sqrt{19}}6$. Multiply by $2x$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x^2&=10x-1\\\\6x^2-10x+1&=0\\\\a&=6,\\quad b=-10,\\quad c=1\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-10)\\pm\\sqrt{(-10)^2-4(6)(1)}}{2(6)}\\\\x&=\\frac{10\\pm\\sqrt{76}}{12}\\\\x&=\\frac{5\\pm\\sqrt{19}}6\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{5k+7}{k-1}=3k+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=-1$ or $3$. Clear the denominator to obtain $3k^2-6k-9=0$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $k\\ne1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}5k+7&=(3k+2)(k-1)\\\\5k+7&=3k^2-k-2\\\\3k^2-6k-9&=0\\\\a&=3,\\quad b=-6,\\quad c=-9\\\\k&=\\frac{-(-6)\\pm\\sqrt{(-6)^2-4(3)(-9)}}{2(3)}\\\\k&=\\frac{6\\pm12}6\\\\k&=-1\\text{ or }3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{u+3}{2u-7}=\\dfrac{2u-1}{u-3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$u=\\dfrac43$ or $4$. Clear the denominators to obtain $3u^2-16u+16=0$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $u\\ne\\frac72,3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(u+3)(u-3)&=(2u-1)(2u-7)\\\\u^2-9&=4u^2-16u+7\\\\3u^2-16u+16&=0\\\\a&=3,\\quad b=-16,\\quad c=16\\\\u&=\\frac{-(-16)\\pm\\sqrt{(-16)^2-4(3)(16)}}{2(3)}\\\\u&=\\frac{16\\pm8}6\\\\u&=\\frac43\\text{ or }4\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restrictions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$2(k-1)=\\dfrac{4-5k}{k+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=\\dfrac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{73}}4$. Clear the denominator to obtain $2k^2+5k-6=0$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $k\\ne-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(k-1)(k+1)&=4-5k\\\\2k^2-2&=4-5k\\\\2k^2+5k-6&=0\\\\a&=2,\\quad b=5,\\quad c=-6\\\\k&=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{5^2-4(2)(-6)}}{2(2)}\\\\k&=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{73}}4\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-m",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac2{a+3}+\\dfrac{a+3}2=\\dfrac{10}3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-\\dfrac73$ or $3$. Multiply by $6(a+3)$ to obtain $3a^2-2a-21=0$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $a\\ne-3$. Multiply by $6(a+3)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}12+3(a+3)^2&=20(a+3)\\\\12+3a^2+18a+27&=20a+60\\\\3a^2-2a-21&=0\\\\a&=\\frac{-(-2)\\pm\\sqrt{(-2)^2-4(3)(-21)}}{2(3)}\\\\a&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{256}}6\\\\a&=\\frac{2\\pm16}6\\\\a&=-\\frac73\\text{ or }3\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic coefficients are $3,-2,-21$. Both solutions satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-n",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3t}{t^2-6}=\\sqrt3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=2\\sqrt3$ or $-\\sqrt3$. Clear the denominator and divide by $\\sqrt3$ to obtain $t^2-\\sqrt3t-6=0$.",
          "worked": "Require $t\\ne\\pm\\sqrt6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3t&=\\sqrt3(t^2-6)\\\\t^2-\\sqrt3t-6&=0\\\\a&=1,\\quad b=-\\sqrt3,\\quad c=-6\\\\t&=\\frac{-(-\\sqrt3)\\pm\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt3)^2-4(1)(-6)}}{2(1)}\\\\t&=\\frac{\\sqrt3\\pm\\sqrt{27}}2\\\\t&=\\frac{\\sqrt3\\pm3\\sqrt3}2\\\\t&=2\\sqrt3\\text{ or }-\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restrictions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q13-o",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "o",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3m+1}{3m-1}-\\dfrac{3m-1}{3m+1}=2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$m=\\dfrac{1\\pm\\sqrt2}3$. Clear the denominators to obtain $9m^2-6m-1=0$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Require $m\\ne\\pm\\frac13$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(3m+1)^2-(3m-1)^2&=2(3m-1)(3m+1)\\\\12m&=18m^2-2\\\\9m^2-6m-1&=0\\\\a&=9,\\quad b=-6,\\quad c=-1\\\\m&=\\frac{-(-6)\\pm\\sqrt{(-6)^2-4(9)(-1)}}{2(9)}\\\\m&=\\frac{6\\pm\\sqrt{72}}{18}\\\\m&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt2}3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth solutions satisfy the restrictions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      }
    ]
